# Findings adjudicated and rejected, with the reason. One `<path>: <title>` per line.

# PR #69 (issue #60). Half of this does not hold: `followUpComplete` already requires
# `nextStep == null`, so a stale PENDING job blocks the completion marker on its own, with or
# without the paused flag. The other half is real but predates this PR and is independent of
# appointments: the job branch of the estimate does not mirror the handler's gates (agent.enabled,
# isTestSilenced, step existence, the episode check, shouldBotHandle), so a stale job shows a
# phantom countdown even with no appointment anywhere. That is a separate defect in the estimate
# itself and belongs in its own change, not folded into the appointment flag. Filed as #72.
src/modules/conversations/service.ts: Validate pending jobs before marking the sequence paused

# PR #75 (issue #61). Real, and it predates this PR: `updateMirror` writes status/assignee and never
# `lastEventAt`, so the guard this change replaces (`existing.lastEventAt > newLastEventAt`) did not
# reject an in-flight conversation event after a console write either. The one sub-case where the old
# guard did reject it — a message landed in between and moved `lastEventAt` — is the exact discard
# that leaves a delayed handoff lost forever, i.e. issue #61 itself; the two cannot both hold.
# Closing it needs the version our own write produced, and the two endpoints it calls do not return
# it (`assignments#create` renders the agent; `toggle_status` renders success/conversation_id/
# current_status/snoozed_until). The REST `show` DOES render it, though
# (`conversations/partials/_conversation.json.jbuilder`), so the fix is a re-read after the write
# rather than a fork change — one extra call per console action, which is its own scope. The
# marker-based attempt at doing it without any version was built and removed inside this PR after
# review found four races in it. Filed as #77.
src/modules/chatwoot/mirror.ts: Fence source events after locally written state
src/modules/chatwoot/state-order.ts: Fence source events after locally written state

# PR #75 (issue #61). The gap is real — while the handoff's own event is delayed, the mirror does not
# know about the human, and a turn already running rechecks the ROW — but the remedy is not available
# yet. Trusting a versioned message snapshot for the assignee undoes a take-over made from our own
# console: that write claims no version, so the row sits ahead of its marks and the tail carries a
# HIGHER version with an OLDER truth. Measured, not argued: applying the suggested change turns "a
# take-over in the console survives a message tail from before it" red. Both failure modes end the
# same way (the bot answers over a human); this one is bounded by the webhook's own retry budget
# (AgentBots::WebhookJob, 3 attempts 3s apart), while the console one lasts until the echo arrives.
# #77 is what unblocks it: once a local write claims the version it produced (the REST show renders
# `updated_at`), the row is never ahead of its marks and a newer versioned snapshot stops being
# ambiguous. Then this change becomes correct, and desirable.
src/modules/chatwoot/mirror.ts: Mirror newer human ownership from message events
src/modules/chatwoot/state-order.ts: Mirror newer human ownership from message events
